id=a52sxq_settings_search_speed
name=Settings search: results without waiting for the per-open re-index
author=kusti420
description=SecSettingsIntelligence re-indexes every time search opens (DatabaseIndexingManager.IndexingTask: Settings dynamic raw data, tags, breadcrumbs, in parallel with the ~5 s AsyncNonIndexableIndexingTask that asks every Settings fragment for its non-indexable keys) and SearchFragment.handleQueryText dropped typed queries until that finished (~3.3 s on the A52s). When the refresh is not a full index (same fingerprint/locale/provider packages, essential indexing finished before) queries now run at once against the existing WAL database; the stock requery in onEssentialIndexingFinished still refreshes the list when the re-index ends, so the final results are identical to stock. sec_dynamic_prefs_index, which the refresh used to drop at its start and refill seconds later, is now emptied inside the refill transaction so an early query never sees it empty. Full indexes (new build, locale change, provider package change) keep the stock wait. Which settings are searchable is not changed. K4SearchSpeed.smali is generated from src/ (javac + d8 + baksmali).
